# The cheat sequence state 0x43bb70 / 0x43bb74 (DragonState CheatState / CheatMode) is written only by the cheat-letter handler (listing
# pbctrl_bdoor_controller, FT 0x4282c0): neither a new ball nor a player change resets it, so a half-typed sequence of player 1 is completed by player 2.
# Control: a lone X at mode 2 does nothing (the X case needs the last accepted letter A, bb70 == 0x41), mode stays 2. Player 1 then types N, M, A (bb70 = A,
# bb74 = 2 = the NMAX family). Switch to player 2 (info_text_box message_field set to 2 and a_kout2.message_field to 5 there, as the per-player values are P2's own):
# the single X completes NMAX and StartSelectedQuest starts mode 5, with ball_held 1 (as d_nmax). A reset of the cheat state per player would leave mode 2.
# The `type` frames are the key-to-message latency of the hook (d_nmax: NMAX typed at 420 acts at 423): expects sit 50 frames after each type.
init window 960 666
init fixed_dt 10
init seed 1
init option Players 2
init dump_period 100
10 key down new_game
11 key up new_game
200 key down plunger
300 key up plunger
400 event a_spot4 ControlCollision
410 poke a_kout2 message_field 5
420 type X
470 expect mode == 2
480 type NMA
540 expect mode == 2
560 msg table SwitchToNextPlayer 0
600 poke info_text_box message_field 2
601 poke a_kout2 message_field 5
610 expect mode == 2
620 type X
680 expect mode == 5
680 expect ball_held == 1
700 quit
